@copilot Add a focused regression test for the gRPC response-header context fix already in this PR. Use a real successful RPC through the instrumented client and observe the application-facing `ClientCall.Listener.onHeaders` callback. Assert that it sees the exact caller span captured when creating the call, not the outgoing gRPC CLIENT span, and that a custom OpenTelemetry context value is preserved. Make sure the callback actually ran, and collect its observations for assertions on the test thread. The test should fail before the `onHeaders` override and pass with it.

Reuse the existing gRPC test setup where practical. `instrumentation/grpc-1.6/testing/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/grpc/v1_6/AbstractGrpcTest.java` has a `userContextPreserved` test, but its `StreamObserver.onNext` assertion does not exercise response headers. Keep this scoped to regression coverage; do not change production behavior. Run the relevant focused Gradle test and demonstrate that it catches the pre-fix behavior if feasible.

Update this existing PR directly on `open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation:otelbot/instruction-audit-45426016089`; do not open a separate PR as a workaround. Keep the branch GitHub assigns you if the platform creates a follow-up branch. Do not rename it or create a replacement branch.

